                        <div data-id="377" class="accordion-content px-4 text-sm text-txt-muted"><p data-id="378" class="pb-4">Incidental findings on imaging can lead to catastrophizing, increased fear-avoidance behavior, and longer recovery times. Patients may believe their spine is "damaged" and avoid normal activity, which worsens outcomes.</p></div>
